WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.911
Step four runs the smoke test,

2
00:00:01.911 --> 00:00:06.563
on the fixture validation kit run and
the other kits' fixture provenance.

3
00:00:06.563 --> 00:00:11.099
It reads the gates' checks again after
the change, and answers go or no-go.

4
00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:14.256
It checks that the kit run
matches its own manifest,

5
00:00:14.256 --> 00:00:17.563
and it notes fixture mode, so
the tenant isn't compared.

6
00:00:17.563 --> 00:00:18.824
Then the failures.

7
00:00:18.824 --> 00:00:27.800
Three checks fail: VK-HR-01,
VK-DG-01 and VK-CA-01.

8
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.725
VK-NPI-03 ended in Error.

9
00:00:31.725 --> 00:00:36.738
And the HR dry run has nine rows
quarantined, against a limit of zero.

10
00:00:36.738 --> 00:00:39.625
You'll recognize those
from Modules 1 and 8.

11
00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:42.487
Every change has a
rollback, so that passes.

12
00:00:42.487 --> 00:00:47.912
The answer is NO-GO, five failed, in
fixture mode, and the exit code is two.

13
00:00:47.912 --> 00:00:50.438
The fixtures carry findings on purpose.

14
00:00:50.438 --> 00:00:52.981
The report's hash changes with each run,

15
00:00:52.981 --> 00:00:56.930
because the report records when
it ran, so it isn't shown here.
